name=Assignment-5.1.md Assignment 5.1 — Convert an HTML Page into a Styled Page[cite: 21] What to build: Add CSS to the HTML website from Week 4[cite: 21]. Steps:Create a style.css file[cite: 21].Link the external stylesheet in HTML[cite: 21].Set the body background, text color, and font[cite: 21].Style headings, paragraphs, and links[cite: 21].Make navigation links readable and attractive[cite: 21].Inspect styles using Chrome DevTools[cite: 21]. Submission: Styled version of the original HTML page and the CSS file[cite: 21].
Here is a clean, modern external CSS stylesheet and a matching semantic HTML structural template. The CSS transitions the basic layout into a professional, attractive workspace with clear contrast, a modern sans-serif typeface hierarchy, and styled navigation targets.

1. The External Stylesheet (style.css)

css
/* ==========================================================================
   Base Elements Setup
   ========================================================================== */
body {
    background-color: #f8fafc; /* Subtle, clean light gray background */
    color: #1e293b;            /* High-contrast charcoal slate text */
    font-family: 'Segoe UI', system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif;
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
}

/* ==========================================================================
   Typography Configurations
   ========================================================================== */
h1, h2, h3 {
    color: #0f172a;            /* Darker tone for standout headers */
    margin-top: 0;
}

h1 {
    font-size: 2.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
}

h2 {
    font-size: 1.75rem;
    border-bottom: 2px solid #e2e8f0;
    padding-bottom: 8px;
    margin-top: 2rem;
}

p {
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
}

/* Base link behavior */
a {
    color: #2563eb;            /* Bright interactive blue */
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: color 0.2s ease-in-out;
}

a:hover {
    color: #1d4ed8;            /* Darker blue emphasis on hover */
    text-decoration: underline;
}

/* ==========================================================================
   Header & Navigation Styling (Readable and Attractive)
   ========================================================================== */
header {
    background-color: #0f172a; /* Deep structural dark navy background */
    color: #ffffff;
    text-align: center;
    padding: 40px 20px 20px 20px;
}

nav {
    background-color: #1e293b; /* Accent dark slate block */
    padding: 0 10px;
}

nav ul {
    list-style-type: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 15px;
}

nav li {
    margin: 0;
}

nav a {
    color: #f1f5f9;            /* Light gray text for visibility */
    display: block;
    padding: 14px 20px;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
}

nav a:hover {
    background-color: #334155; /* Interactive hover block effect */
    color: #38bdf8;            /* Bright sky blue highlighting color */
    text-decoration: none;
}

/* ==========================================================================
   Main Content Layout Structural Block
   ========================================================================== */
main {
    max-width: 800px;
    margin: 40px auto;
    padding: 0 20px;
}

/* ==========================================================================
   Footer Elements
   ========================================================================== */
footer {
    background-color: #0f172a;
    color: #94a3b8;
    text-align: center;
    padding: 20px;
    margin-top: 60px;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
}
Use code with caution.

